    "explanation": "To the rider: you are right that the price you locked at booking was not the price you were charged, and that is the one thing this ruling fixes. EV-FARE-00506 records an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip with quoted_fare_sgd of 45.00 against total_charged of 55.20 — an excess of 10.20. POL-RD-11(a) refunds that excess in full, less only the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable on top of the quote, and on this ledger there are none: tolls_erp 0.00 with an empty erp_gantries list, waiting_time_fee 0.00, and airport_surcharge 0.00 — a Changi surcharge is chargeable only on a trip ORIGINATING at the airport, and this trip ended at Changi T3, so none is properly chargeable in any event. The refundable figure therefore stays the whole 10.20, and it already sits on a 0.05 boundary. The balance of the 55.20 stands. On an upfront-quoted trip the distance and time lines are fixed at booking, so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available to you however the trip was driven; your premise that the booking price was locked is correct, and it is precisely why the only money that moves is the gap above the quote. To the driver: nothing in this ruling is a finding against you. The governing trace (EV-GPS-00506, weight 1.0; 145 fixes, 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, zero gaps, max gap 0 s) measures trace_distance_km 19.76 against optimal_distance_km 19.60 — an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.82% — below both POL-RD-01 gates of 0.8 km and 20%, and gps_trace.trace_distance_km governs over the rounded trip_record copy of 19.8 km, so no deviation is established and POL-RD-02 never runs. The 10.20 is a reconciliation between the platform's quote and the platform's own rate-card charge, not a penalty on your driving, and it is not netted against you. On the driver's-side claims: your POL-RD-01 no-deviation claim is accepted, and the same finding disposes of your POL-RD-11 claims that no distance-or-time refund is available and that the outer limit of any correction is the 10.20 gap; your POL-RD-07 claim that the trace is not policy-impaired is accepted (no limb (a)-(c) fires); your POL-RD-08 claim that the rider's threshold burden is not discharged is accepted and is consistent with this outcome, since the money moved rests on the quote/charge comparison, which requires no excess; your POL-RD-06 claim is accepted — no MATERIAL deviation exists, and even on the named fields driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, so no pattern is established, no limb (b) uplift is available and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is warranted; your POL-RD-10 claim is accepted — identifiers match, timestamps run forward, no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact, and every charge line has its counterpart — so no escalation trigger fires and the case is ruled rather than held. The rider's POL-RD-11 claim for the 10.20 excess is accepted and is the ruling; the rider's POL-RD-09/POL-RD-11 claim that no pass-through line is added back is accepted; the rider's POL-RD-08 claim that the artifacts describe one trip and that the deviation_claims_60d overlay is not engaged is accepted. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance of 19.8 km is not less than the traced 19.76 km, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb has no shortfall to compute, and no gantry or surcharge line fails POL-RD-09(4), so there is no billing-integrity referral. Driver compensation is null. On the profiles: EV-DPROF-00506 and EV-RPROF-00506 were used only as credibility context. Their rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation rates, acceptance rate, active region and the lifetime counters prior_deviation_flags and prior_disputes_filed are context-only under POL-GEN-01 and decided nothing; only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d (POL-RD-06) and deviation_claims_60d (POL-RD-08) were consulted, and neither side's near-synonym arguments were given weight. EV-ADVIS-00506-01 is a MISSING traffic advisory at weight 0.0; it carries no fact, no exculpatory clause was invoked against it, and POL-RD-10(5) is therefore not engaged. The ruling rests on EV-FARE-00506 at weight 1.0, so confidence is 0.90."
