    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the driving on this trip is clean, and only the billing is not.\n\nOn the route, the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00506, 145 fixes at a 10-second cadence, zero gaps, weight 1.0) measures 19.76 km against the booked optimal of 19.60 km recorded on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00506, routing-engine-v3.2). That is an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.82% — far below both POL-RD-01 gates of 0.8 km and 20%, and the trace governs that measurement. The ride took the booked 24.0 minutes, waiting was 1.0 minute and billed at 0.00, no ERP or toll line was charged, and the in-app chat log (EV-CHAT-00506) is complete, untruncated and empty. Both advocates agree on this, and so do I: no deviation is established, no exoneration clause (POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05) needs to run, and the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00506-01, weight 0.0) is invoked by nobody and carries nothing. Because there is no deviation, the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered at all, and in any event the only two fields that clause names show nothing — deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d 250, against thresholds of 3 flags or a 0.05 ratio — so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arise. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, no interval over 30 s), and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the identifiers all read TRP-00506, the timestamps run forward consistently, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor.\n\nThe money does not match the contract. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00506) records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 45.00, but total_charged 55.20, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. On an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking, so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available however the route went — which is exactly why the rider's own claim rests on the quote, not on the driving. What POL-RD-11(a) gives the rider is the amount by which the charge exceeds the quote plus any properly chargeable pass-throughs. Those pass-throughs are all nil: tolls_erp 0.00 with an empty erp_gantries list, airport_surcharge 0.00 (and not chargeable in any case, because this trip ENDS at Changi T3 and does not originate there), and waiting_time_fee 0.00. The excess is therefore 55.20 − 45.00 = 10.20, refunded in full; it already sits on a 0.05 boundary, so rounding changes nothing. The rider is right as to that 10.20 and unsupported as to the remaining 45.00 of the 55.20 contested, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\nThe driver is also right on his own point: the 10.20 is a quote-versus-charge mismatch on the platform's ledger (EV-FARE-00506) and nothing in the record attributes any part of it to his driving, so no adverse finding attaches to him, no driver compensation is claimed or due (the billed 19.8 km exceeds the traced 19.76 km, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb has nothing behind it), and no referral is produced by any clause — POL-RD-09(4) has no phantom gantry or misplaced surcharge line to act on, and POL-RD-06(c) has no pattern to act on. Profile material was used only for the counters a clause names (deviation_flags_90d, completed_trips_90d, deviation_claims_60d); rating, account age, lifetime trips, acceptance rate, prior_deviation_flags and the other context-only fields were treated as context only. There is one open question for the platform rather than for the parties: why an upfront-quoted trip was charged 10.20 above its own lock-in price, and whether the distance_fare and time_fare lines on this ledger reconcile with rate card RC-SG-2026Q3-RYDEXL — that is for the fare-model owner to look at, and it does not hold up this refund.",
